NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008325 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008326 "=head2 Support"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008327 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008328 "My consulting company, Data Plan Services, offers annual and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008329 "multi-annual support contracts for the DBI. These provide sustained"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008330 "support for DBI development, and sustained value for you in return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008331 "Contact me for details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008332 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008333 "=head2 Sponsor Enhancements"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008334 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008335 "If your company would benefit from a specific new DBI feature,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008336 "please consider sponsoring its development.  Work is performed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008337 "rapidly, and usually on a fixed-price payment-on-delivery basis."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008338 "Contact me for details."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008339 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008340 "Using such targeted financing allows you to contribute to DBI"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008341 "development, and rapidly get something specific and valuable in return."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008342 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008343 "=head1 ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008344 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008345 "I would like to acknowledge the valuable contributions of the many"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008346 "people I have worked with on the DBI project, especially in the early"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008347 "years (1992-1994). In no particular order: Kevin Stock, Buzz Moschetti,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008348 "Kurt Andersen, Ted Lemon, William Hails, Garth Kennedy, Michael Peppler,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008349 "Neil S. Briscoe, Jeff Urlwin, David J. Hughes, Jeff Stander,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008350 "Forrest D Whitcher, Larry Wall, Jeff Fried, Roy Johnson, Paul Hudson,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008351 "Georg Rehfeld, Steve Sizemore, Ron Pool, Jon Meek, Tom Christiansen,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008352 "Steve Baumgarten, Randal Schwartz, and a whole lot more."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008353 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008354 "Then, of course, there are the poor souls who have struggled through"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008355 "untold and undocumented obstacles to actually implement DBI drivers."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008356 "Among their ranks are Jochen Wiedmann, Alligator Descartes, Jonathan"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008357 "Leffler, Jeff Urlwin, Michael Peppler, Henrik Tougaard, Edwin Pratomo,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008358 "Davide Migliavacca, Jan Pazdziora, Peter Haworth, Edmund Mergl, Steve"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008359 "Williams, Thomas Lowery, and Phlip Plumlee. Without them, the DBI would"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008360 "not be the practical reality it is today.  I'm also especially grateful"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008361 "to Alligator Descartes for starting work on the first edition of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008362 "\"Programming the Perl DBI\" book and letting me jump on board."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008363 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008364 "The DBI and DBD::Oracle were originally developed while I was Technical"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008365 "Director (CTO) of the Paul Ingram Group in the UK.  So I'd especially like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008366 "to thank Paul for his generosity and vision in supporting this work for many years."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008367 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008368 "A couple of specific DBI features have been sponsored by enlightened companies:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008369 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008370 "The development of the swap_inner_handle() method was sponsored by BizRate.com (L<http://BizRate.com>)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008371 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008372 "The development of DBD::Gofer and related modules was sponsored by Shopzilla.com (L<https::connexity.com>)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008373 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008374 "=head1 CONTRIBUTING"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008375 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008376 "As you can see above, many people have contributed to the DBI and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008377 "drivers in many ways over many years."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008378 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008379 "If you'd like to help then see L<http://dbi.perl.org/contributing>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008380 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008381 "If you'd like the DBI to do something new or different then a good way"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008382 "to make that happen is to do it yourself and send me a patch to the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008383 "source code that shows the changes. (But read \"Speak before you patch\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008384 "below.)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008385 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008386 "=head2 Browsing the source code repository"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008387 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008388 "Use https://github.com/perl5-dbi/dbi"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008389 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008390 "=head2 How to create a patch using Git"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008391 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008392 "The DBI source code is maintained using Git.  To access the source"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008393 "you'll need to install a Git client. Then, to get the source code, do:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008394 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008395 "  git clone https://github.com/perl5-dbi/dbi.git DBI-git"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008396 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008397 "The source code will now be available in the new subdirectory C<DBI-git>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008398 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008399 "When you want to synchronize later, issue the command"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008400 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008401 "  git pull --all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008402 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008403 "Make your changes, test them, test them again until everything passes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008404 "If there are no tests for the new feature you added or a behaviour change,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008405 "the change should include a new test. Then commit the changes. Either use"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008406 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008407 "  git gui"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008408 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008409 "or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008410 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008411 "  git commit -a -m 'Message to my changes'"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008412 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008413 "If you get any conflicts reported you'll need to fix them first."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008414 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008415 "Then generate the patch file to be mailed:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008416 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008417 "  git format-patch -1 --attach"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008418 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008419 "which will create a file 0001-*.patch (where * relates to the commit message)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008420 "Read the patch file, as a sanity check, and then email it to dbi-dev@perl.org."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008421 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008422 "If you have a L<github|https://github.com> account, you can also fork the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008423 "repository, commit your changes to the forked repository and then do a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008424 "pull request."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008425 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008426 "=head2 How to create a patch without Git"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008427 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008428 "Unpack a fresh copy of the distribution:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008429 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008430 "  wget http://cpan.metacpan.org/authors/id/T/TI/TIMB/DBI-1.627.tar.gz"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008431 "  tar xfz DBI-1.627.tar.gz"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008432 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008433 "Rename the newly created top level directory:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008434 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008435 "  mv DBI-1.627 DBI-1.627.your_foo"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008436 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008437 "Edit the contents of DBI-1.627.your_foo/* till it does what you want."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008438 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008439 "Test your changes and then remove all temporary files:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008440 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008441 "  make test && make distclean"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008442 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008443 "Go back to the directory you originally unpacked the distribution:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008444 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008445 "  cd .."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008446 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008447 "Unpack I<another> copy of the original distribution you started with:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008448 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008449 "  tar xfz DBI-1.627.tar.gz"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008450 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008451 "Then create a patch file by performing a recursive C<diff> on the two"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008452 "top level directories:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008453 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008454 "  diff -purd DBI-1.627 DBI-1.627.your_foo > DBI-1.627.your_foo.patch"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008455 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008456 "=head2 Speak before you patch"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008457 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008458 "For anything non-trivial or possibly controversial it's a good idea"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008459 "to discuss (on dbi-dev@perl.org) the changes you propose before"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008460 "actually spending time working on them. Otherwise you run the risk"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008461 "of them being rejected because they don't fit into some larger plans"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008462 "you may not be aware of."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008463 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008464 "You can also reach the developers on IRC (chat). If they are on-line,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008465 "the most likely place to talk to them is the #dbi channel on irc.perl.org"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008466 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008467 "=head1 TRANSLATIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008468 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008469 "A German translation of this manual (possibly slightly out of date) is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008470 "available, thanks to O'Reilly, at:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008471 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008472 "  http://www.oreilly.de/catalog/perldbiger/"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008473 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008474 "=head1 OTHER RELATED WORK AND PERL MODULES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008475 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008476 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008477 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008478 "=item L<Apache::DBI>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008479 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008480 "To be used with the Apache daemon together with an embedded Perl"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008481 "interpreter like C<mod_perl>. Establishes a database connection which"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008482 "remains open for the lifetime of the HTTP daemon. This way the CGI"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008483 "connect and disconnect for every database access becomes superfluous."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008484 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008485 "=item SQL Parser"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008486 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008487 "See also the L<SQL::Statement> module, SQL parser and engine."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008488 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008489 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008490 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008491 "=head1 TODO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008492 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008493 "=head2 Documentation"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008494 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008495 "These entries are still to be written:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008496 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008497 "=over 2"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008498 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008499 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008500 "=item DBIf_TRACE_CON"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008501 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008502 "=item DBIf_TRACE_DBD"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008503 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008504 "=item DBIf_TRACE_ENC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00008505 ""
